-- bank.lekh: a bank account with safe error handling (no crashes, no null)

record Account:
    owner as text
    balance as number

to deposit changeable account as Account, amount as number gives result of number:
    if amount is at most 0:
        give back problem "a deposit must be more than 0 (got {amount})"
    increase account's balance by amount
    give back ok account's balance

to withdraw changeable account as Account, amount as number gives result of number:
    if amount is greater than account's balance:
        give back problem "not enough money: {account's owner} has {account's balance}, asked for {amount}"
    decrease account's balance by amount
    give back ok account's balance

-- `try` means: if this is a problem, stop here and pass the problem up
to transfer changeable source as Account, changeable target as Account, amount as number gives result of number:
    try withdraw with lend source, amount
    try deposit with lend target, amount
    give back ok amount

-- turning user text into a safe number
to parse_amount input as text gives result of number:
    let amount be try input as number
    if amount is less than 0: give back problem "amounts can't be negative"
    give back ok amount

let changeable mine be an Account with owner "Sushant", balance 100
let changeable savings be an Account with owner "Savings", balance 0

when deposit with lend mine, 50:
    is ok balance: say "Deposited 50. Balance is now {balance}."
    is problem why: say "Deposit failed: {why}"

when withdraw with lend mine, 500:
    is ok balance: say "Withdrew 500. Balance is now {balance}."
    is problem why: say "Withdrawal failed: {why}"

when transfer with lend mine, lend savings, 120:
    is ok moved: say "Moved {moved} to savings."
    is problem why: say "Transfer failed: {why}"

-- `or else` gives a fallback value when something goes wrong
let attempt be withdraw with lend mine, 1000 or else -1
say "Big withdrawal result: {attempt}"

for each typed in list of "25", "abc", "-5":
    when parse_amount of typed:
        is ok amount: say "'{typed}' -> {amount}"
        is problem why: say "'{typed}' rejected: {why}"

say "Final: {mine's owner} has {mine's balance}, savings has {savings's balance}."
